## Third-party code

`vendor/pamela/` is NOT covered by the copyright line above. It is vendored
upstream code from the PAMELA project by Tomáš Bruckner, reused verbatim under
its own MIT license:

  Copyright (c) 2026 Tomáš Bruckner

  Single-token output distributions as behavioral fingerprints of large
  language models — software. DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.21278793

The full license text and the provenance note for it are in
`vendor/pamela/LICENSE`; what was vendored, and whether each file was modified,
is recorded in `vendor/pamela/ATTRIBUTION.md`.

The paper's dataset (DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.21278557) is CC-BY-4.0 and is NOT
redistributed here — `npm run fetch-data` downloads it from Zenodo at first use.
